# The public archive. This repository is served at samsikallo.github.io/arda-archive,
# so anything committed here is published, and published is not undone by deleting.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL, AND WHY ITS ABSENCE WAS THE WORST OF THE FOUR DEPLOY
# FAULTS. The workshop above has carried a .gitignore for a long time, and its first
# rule is the books: "the books themselves are not ours to redistribute". This
# repository -- the PUBLIC one, the only one that actually publishes -- had no
# .gitignore of any kind. The protection was strongest where the consequence was
# smallest and absent where it was largest.
#
# The workshop's own comment records that three books were once tracked by accident,
# "because one is an .epub and one is a PDF saved with no extension at all", and they
# had to be cut out of history with git filter-branch TWICE, the first pass missing the
# paths they had lived at earlier. That is the cost being guarded against, and it is
# strictly worse here: a private repository can be rewritten quietly, a published one
# has already been fetched.
#
# The pre-commit hook refuses sources/ unconditionally and does not rely on this file.
# Both exist on purpose: the hook stops a deliberate `git add -f`, this stops an
# absent-minded `git add -A`, and neither covers the other's case.

# ---- books, in every form the shelf has ever held one -------------------------------
*.pdf
*.epub
*.mobi
*.azw3
*.djvu
sources/**
"secondary sources"/
secondary sources/

# ---- derived full text: rebuildable, large, and just as much theirs as the books ----
corpus/
*.folded

# ---- what the guards leave behind ---------------------------------------------------
# The deep-link, realms and portrait guards drive a real browser against probe pages
# written beside the real ones. They are removed on a clean run and survive a crash or
# an interrupted suite, which is exactly when someone is most likely to stage broadly.
_*.html

# ---- ordinary noise ------------------------------------------------------------------
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.tree-lease

# THE OWNER RULED ON 29 JULY that the archive does not republish Tolkien's or
# Christopher Tolkien's artwork. arda_traced.svg is 215,090 vector paths traced from his
# published plates -- his linework, not ours -- and it was reachable from map.html behind a
# button reading "Christopher's hand". It stays in the workshop as a research artefact,
# because the archive still measures its own map against his geometry; it is not published.
arda_traced.svg

# THE SAME RULING, ONE STEP FURTHER OUT. arda_his_anchors.json is 161 of Christopher
# Tolkien's label POSITIONS measured off his plates, each tagged hand="Christopher Tolkien"
# and each carrying a `reads` field that TRANSCRIBES WHAT HIS LETTERING SAYS. The archive
# said "his lettering is not reproduced"; this reproduced it in data rather than in type,
# and positions plus transcriptions are a reconstruction of his naming layer whatever they
# are stored as. map.html stopped fetching it when the traced loader was deleted, so it was
# published and serving nothing. It stays in the workshop, with the vectors, for the same
# reason: the archive measures its own map against his and does not republish his.
arda_his_anchors.json

# THE CENTRELINE SHEETS, WITHDRAWN 1 Aug 2026 under the owner's artwork ruling of 29 July:
# "The archive does not republish Tolkien's or Christopher Tolkien's artwork." These eight say in
# their OWN header comments that they are "centrelines of Christopher Tolkien's linework, one path
# per stroke", and they were being SERVED publicly (bel.svg 1.78 MB, gm.svg 3.00 MB, fetched from
# the live site by the Fixer, who found this).
#
# arda_traced.svg was withdrawn under the same ruling and these are the eight sheets it was
# ASSEMBLED FROM. The withdrawal was applied to the assembled file; the parts were never in scope,
# and traced_check's population is that one filename, so nothing could see them. A withdrawal aimed
# at a FILE leaves the SOURCES it was built from.
#
# They stay on disk: the archive still measures its own map against his geometry. What changes is
# that they are not published.
cl/*.svg
